2|0@mormon^1439841362#cu68f8p:laposte$:I had an LDS Social Services therapist tell me this about two years ago. I didn't believe it, so I asked to see the official statement. He didn't have it, but assured me that, "It happened - though it did happen a few years ago, and it is doctrine." I called him out as spouting bull crap, and reported him. I'm not sure if anything happened about it. Following up on him, I did find that there was a letter - the purpose was not to proclaim doctrine from The Lord, but to give guidance to local leaders. And yes, the letter stated as much as OP's statement. It was quickly retracted. Personally, I feel that unless the leadership begins their statement with, "Thus saith The Lord..." everything is opinion - opinion that we can choose to follow or discard. This counts for nearly all that's written in church magazines and said in General Conference. This doesn't mean that we should listen; only that these people are human - like us - and are capable of saying some really stupid stuff. 
